# Continents to rebuild, cheapest first (mbtiles+pbf), one per line.
# The runner re-reads this file before each region, so it can be edited
# freely while the chain is running — never edit the runner itself.
# Comment a line out to skip it; add canada / russia here if wanted.
australia-nz
indian-subcontinent
southeast-asia
south-america
china
africa
united-states
europe
# Added 2026-09-14 on request. Appended rather than inserted in size order:
# the runner holds this file on fd 3 and consumes it line by line, so appends
# are picked up but rewriting earlier lines would corrupt its read position.
# These are NEW regions (never shipped), not refreshes.
russia
canada
# Rebuild: 2026-09-14 build failed validate on two zero-byte satellite
# cache tiles (14/13426/9043-9044). Cache files removed so they re-download;
# create_osm_zim.py now drops empty raster files. Gate-failed ZIM moved to
# rejected-zims/ so the same-name skip in build-region-fast.sh can't fire.
australia-nz
# CORRECTION (2026-09-14, from review): the header above is wrong for the
# runner started 2026-09-14 01:25. That runner holds this file open and reads it
# by byte offset, so ONLY appending whole lines (ending in a newline) is safe
# while it runs. Commenting out, reordering, or atomically replacing this file
# will be missed or corrupt its read. The run-continent-chain.sh installed after
# this note re-reads the list per region, making all of those edits safe for
# any chain launched from now on.
